# F_TRIG, period 100 ms (time is irrelevant to this block).
#
# Derivation: ST body in the standard (ed.3 6.6.3.5.3 table 45):
#   VAR M : BOOL; END_VAR        (* no initial value: M starts FALSE *)
#   Q := NOT CLK AND NOT M;
#   M := NOT CLK;
# and the NOTE under table 45: an F_TRIG "whose CLK input is disconnected
# or is connected to a value of FALSE" has Q at BOOL#1 after its first
# execution following a cold restart, and at BOOL#0 after that. So cycle 0
# (CLK = FALSE, M = FALSE) reports an edge. From then on Q is TRUE for the
# one evaluation in which CLK is FALSE and was TRUE at the previous one.
#
# (Until 2026-11-02 this trace assumed `M : BOOL := TRUE` and had q=FALSE at
# cycle 0; the text of table 45, pointed out on adclz/rk#117, says otherwise.
# See notes/findings.md #6.)
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: clk
outputs: q
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.3.5.3 table 45 (F_TRIG body and NOTE)
---
0 clk=FALSE => q=TRUE
1 clk=TRUE  => q=FALSE
2 clk=FALSE => q=TRUE
3           => q=FALSE
4 clk=TRUE  => q=FALSE
5 clk=TRUE  => q=FALSE
6 clk=FALSE => q=TRUE
7 clk=TRUE  => q=FALSE
8 clk=FALSE => q=TRUE
9 clk=FALSE => q=FALSE
